A||N||19||87ECO5||How do they make their money?||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||02-12-2001||02:02 PM||||My wife's been after me to get a cell phone.  She continues to show me ads from places that promise "free phone, no long distance or roaming charges, no this, no that."  I haven't looked closely at the ads so I haven't seen any fine print.<P>Where are they making their money?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||02-12-2001||02:20 PM||||Flat monthly fee for some amount of minutes plus per minute charge over that. The free phone is usually conditional on signing a 2 or so year contract for the above...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-12-2001||02:21 PM||||They make their money many ways. First, They say it's free but it's not. They give you free air time but there is still a charge for using the regular phone lines. I.E. you call home from the store. Also the free time could only be during non-prime hours. The "line charge" is slightly higher than a regular phone so they sell you the phone and the local phone company pays them. As for "roaming" charges, They don't charge you to use the cells but you still use the regular phone lines too, So they charge you a premium cost. They can also give you the phone for free as long as you sign an agreement for 1 year of service. Which is at a higher rate than normal. Then if you want voice mail, PCS, call waiting, etc they charge you for those.<BR>I have cellular one (now cingular) on a "Digital Family Pak" It's $39.99 per month with 350 free minutes (prime or non-prime) each additional phone is $9.99 and calling from cell phone to cell phone is free all the time. But I still have to pay the line charge. Which is normally $.02 per minute. Some "free" phones have $.11 per minute. Our monthly bill runs about $58.00. So it's $50.00 for the phones but we usually rack up $8.00 in line charges. (Tax is included in that.)<BR>If you want to get a cell phone, get the family pak and get 2 phones. The family pak also sells you all the phones at 50% off.<P>BTW ~ My cell phone is off when I drive (I have voice mail) because I can't stand people who talk and (attempt to) drive.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||02-12-2001||02:55 PM||||I have a Fido "pay-as-you-go" plan, and I only use the phone when I go out.. I leave it off most of the time.<P>My cell phone can make my monitor go crazy (like it's being degaussed) and when I bring the antenna close to it, the screen gets distorted almost as much as a magnet does.. I hate to think what it's doing to my brain when I use it.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||DJRice||02-12-2001||04:37 PM||||Its not free because you buy X amount of minutes for $X per month.  <P>I have a $50 per month for 500 minutes plus unlimited weekend calling for and addtional $10.  I dont have "free weekends" because I pay $10 to have unlimited time.  <P>Make no mistake about it.  If you have a phone, you will get a bill every month.  Its not free.  The exception is those prepaid phones.  You buy time, you talk, you run out of time, and then you buy more.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000005||p4n1c||02-12-2001||04:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>I hate to think what it's doing to my brain when I use it.....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The radiation emitted by newer cell phones is so low that it would take 2 to 3 years of continous use(like beside your head for many hours of each day) to actually do any serious damage.  The 5190 that you have is close to the worse for radiation though(And it's still low).  <P>On Rogers AT&T I got a $100 dollar credit for the phone for signing for 2 years, basically the phone was free, but they just give you a credit to your bill.<P>I like the monthly plan better then pay as you go, because I see pay as you go for kiddies that can't get a monthly plan or people that use the phone for just emergencies.  <P>It's also good to be an employee of a company that is partnered with Rogers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  So you get 20-30% discounts on your bill.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||02-12-2001||04:53 PM||||i bought my phone..then got a plan for 250 minutes for 19.95. It includes all long distance within USA. I can call Hawaii and talk for the whole 250 mins. I got the hook up too so i can plug my laptop in it and get on the forum driving down the road or at a ball game too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||02-12-2001||07:44 PM||||I pay 35 bucks a month for 1500 minutes (500 day time, 1000 nights and weekends..Sprint PCS..theyve gotten alot better)...Ive had my phone for over a year and the only time its ever been turned off was when I dropped it and the battery came off lol. It just stays on constantly...no point in having one if its not on!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||02-12-2001||08:23 PM||||I just got my cell phone bill: $12 acess fee, insurance on the phone $2.95, taxes $0.42 + $1.09+$0.38+ $1.02 for a grand total of $17.86 with no calls made.  I keep it in my car for emergencies.  I use it when I'm on my trips.   When I do use it depending on where I am, its $0.05 - $0.20 per minute, then add in roving charges etc.<BR> The most expensive call that was made was one that was made while I was in Canada.  A call to one of the guys wife when was shopping in the mall while we were at the car show. A 3 minute call was almost $12.  Canada laid some pretty hefty fees on calling within their territory. Plus the roving fees I encountered and international calling charges.  Don't worry they will make money.||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroLisa||02-12-2001||08:26 PM||||I work for Sprint PCS...how they make their money is easy. They sell their phones but you have no contract. When I worked customer service, you wouldnt believe how many people never paid attention to how much they used their phone and had several hundred dollar phone bills every month. If you have a plan, you get x number of minutes but if you go into roaming you pay another $.39/min and if you go over your minutes depending on plan it can be as much as $.25 or so/min.  I can't complain too much, I get 1000 anytime minutes, free long dist/ cheap canada rates ($.12/min) free voicemail/free wireless web...for $75/mo.  But then there's that 1500 min/34.99 plan they have, but problem is, I use a lot of daytime minutes and can't do that since 1250 of the minutes are night/weekend.<BR>anyway, am I babbling yet? I think so  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But as a note Sprint PCS just came up even a couple quarters ago, haven't quite made profit since they are still a new company.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||DJRice||02-12-2001||10:18 PM||||I have a Sprint PCS, and now I have a friend on the inside!  Woohoo!  Lisa, do they have any special super secret promos going? (j/k)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroLisa||02-12-2001||10:39 PM||||You wouldn't believe how many people ask me to get them free phones- I've never even gotten a phone free from them ever- I think I've spent like $500 just on phones in 2 years...ouch. <BR>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000012||onfire||02-13-2001||03:33 AM||||I just got a cel phone from sprint PCS (friday to be exact), and their $49.99 a month for 2000 minutes. 400 min. for day, and 1600 for nights and weekends. Plus free long distance. <P>I do have a ? about the wireless web. If I get on and use it, do they just subtract the minutes, or are they charging me money. I've read through some of there brochures and checked their website. But I can't figure it out.<P>Anyway, they are getting my money.||||reg||5
Z||000013||Oreif||02-13-2001||11:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>I have a Fido "pay-as-you-go" plan, and I only use the phone when I go out.. I leave it off most of the time.<P>My cell phone can make my monitor go crazy (like it's being degaussed) and when I bring the antenna close to it, the screen gets distorted almost as much as a magnet does.. I hate to think what it's doing to my brain when I use it.....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'd say get a different phone. My Nokia is on and sitting in front of my monitor and there is no distortion or color changes. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||02-13-2001||02:31 PM||||My monitor degausses itself every so often anyway, so there's a chance the monitor itself is just really sensitive.. either that or I'm surrounded by high density magnetic fields.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000015||Oreif||02-13-2001||02:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>My monitor degausses itself every so often anyway, so there's a chance the monitor itself is just really sensitive.. either that or I'm surrounded by high density magnetic fields.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The Navy tried that once, Generating a large high density electro-magnetic signal. They thought they could use it to render ships invisible to radar. But it crossed into the space/time continuum and created a portal thru time. Which in turn sucked the USS Nimitz to 1941 the day before Pearl Harbor. But before they could attack the Japanese Navy with F-14's, they turned the machine off and the Nimitz went back to present day. Also turning the machine off sent one of the Navy techs running it into the future where he has remained stuck here until the sequeal (sp?) is made.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>(maybe I have my movies crossed?)<P><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000016||BN Boomer||02-13-2001||02:57 PM||||<I>(maybe I have my movies crossed?)</I><P>It would appear so. Sounds like a combination of The Philadelphia Experiment and The Final Countdown.||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroLisa||02-13-2001||04:04 PM||||onfire:<BR>its depends on what you signed up for when you got your plan. When I upped my plan, I opted for "free wireless web" that means I can use however much wireless web I want- and it doesn't cost me money, just goes out of my minutes per month. I have a 1000 minute plan, so if I use 200 on WW, I have 800 to talk. If you chose free voice command (really cool by the way) you can pay I think $10 a month for WW and it still just takes out of your minutes.<BR>A<BR>nd a question I had, but got answered was if you turn on AIM on your phone, you are only charged minutes when you are on WW. If you close the phone (or hit end and see the normal time stamp), technically your not being charged for WW until someone IMs you and you hit "accept" and get connected. Make sense?<P>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000018||onfire||02-14-2001||03:01 PM||||FeiroLisa makes sense to me.<P>I am on their $49.99 for 2000 minutes plan. It doen't say anything about free Wireless Web, so I think I have to pay the 10 bucks a month for it. I don't really need it, so i'm not to worried about it.||||reg||1
Z||000019||FieroLisa||02-14-2001||05:03 PM||||onfire: if you do ever choose to use wireless web its going to cost you something like $.39/min.<BR>I guess with all their new plans available, they arent offering all the free options they were. Just a few mos ago I was paying the same amount as you with only a quarter of the minutes ($49.99/500 min)<BR>I'm a little rusty on this, I haven't worked there in a few mos. and I probably won't go back until next quarter.<P>Lisa||||reg||1
